<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the index is valid, non-negative, and not greater than the initial size of the list, and the role is not null, then for every position from 0 up to, but not including, the index, the element at that position remains unchanged or continues to be null after the insertion.
